1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,000
When you make a uniform skirt, you will usually encounter problems such as uneven folding and irregularity.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:21,000
As shown in the video, there will be irregularities after the skirt is made.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The reason for these problems is that the skirt is folded while imitating the sewing line.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Let's do an example.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:43,000
You may arrange the skirt pattern at the point of arrangement around the skirt, and then sew up these patterns.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000
After this operation, there will be irregularity after the skirt is opened.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,000
This is because there is an irregularity after the skirt is opened.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,000
This is because there is an irregularity after the skirt is opened.

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:58,000
When making a skirt, the skirt itself has a sewing line, and the skirt does not have the folding angle yet.

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The skirt cannot be folded well under the function of the sewing line.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The solution to this problem is very simple, which is to fold the skirt first.

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Here we have added the sewing line, so we need to temporarily anti-activate these sewing lines.

13
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Click and drag the mouse button at the 2D window to select all the sewing lines here in the skirt and anti-activate.

14
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Then in the 3D window, it is best not to have an intersection between the panels, otherwise it may not be stable.

15
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:34,000
The hard-painted panel can apply a very hard fabric to the panel, and the fold is also easier to appear.

16
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The sewing line between the panels also needs to be anti-activated, and then you can start to simulate.

17
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,000
At this time, the panel will be folded.

18
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:49,000
In order to prevent the panel from falling to the ground, you can pull it higher and simulate it again.

19
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:59,000
If the panel is folded more accurately, then activate the sewing line.

20
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:14,000
After folding, activate the sewing line.

21
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Pay attention to check if there is any part of the waist belt that has not been anti-activated.

22
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
After all is activated, you can start to simulate.

23
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
The sewing line will work again.

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Please activate the side sewing line at the end.

25
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Sometimes the panel is relatively large, and it may be more or less, and it will be interspersed.

26
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,000
If the side sewing line is activated, there may be an unstable problem.

27
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Then solve the hardening, let the panel fall naturally, and then activate the side sewing line.

28
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Then it is sort of finished.

29
